---
import ExcludedDocumentsList from "../components/ExcludedDocumentsList.astro";
import LegalDocument from "../components/LegalDocument.astro";
import MarketingPageShell from "../components/MarketingPageShell.astro";
import {
	DODO_PAYMENTS,
	EXCLUDED_DOCUMENTS_INTRO_TERMS,
	LEGAL_OPERATOR,
} from "../config/legal-content";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Terms of Service - Filosign"
	description="Terms for Filosign document signing software and attached payout workflows."
>
	<MarketingPageShell>
			<LegalDocument
				title="Terms of Service"
				description="Terms for Filosign document workflow software and optional payout attachment. Not legal advice - review with counsel before production launch."
				lastUpdated="May 2026"
			>
				<h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
				<p>
					By accessing or using Filosign, you agree to these Terms, our <a
						href="/privacy"
						class="underline">Privacy Policy</a
					>, our <a href="/acceptable-use" class="underline"
						>Acceptable Use Policy</a
					> (the "<strong>Acceptable Use Policy</strong>"), and any product limits
					shown in the service.
				</p>
				<p>
					If you use Filosign for an organization, you represent that you have
					authority to bind that organization and manage documents, recipients,
					payments, and subscriptions on its behalf.
				</p>

				<h2>2. Product Stage and Environments</h2>
				<p>
					We operate two distinct environments of the Service:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Production Environment:</strong> Running on Base Mainnet. This environment is intended for real, sensitive, and confidential agreements. Access is subject to paid subscription entitlements managed by {DODO_PAYMENTS.name} as the Merchant of Record.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Sandbox Environment:</strong> Running on Base Sepolia (Testnet). This environment is provided strictly for free testing, evaluation, and demonstration purposes. No real funds are used, and no warranties of any kind are provided. We reserve the right to wipe Sandbox data, clear user accounts, and modify Sandbox state at any time without notice or liability. Do not upload sensitive or confidential documents to the Sandbox environment.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>3. Eligibility and accounts</h2>
				<p>
					You must be at least 18 years old, or the age required for the
					service to lawfully process your data in your jurisdiction. You may
					use Filosign as an individual, professional, or organization, but you
					are responsible for complying with laws that apply to your use.
				</p>
				<p>
					You are responsible for your account, wallet, authentication method,
					recovery materials, transactions, documents, recipients, and activity
					under your account. Do not use Filosign if you are legally prohibited
					from doing so.
				</p>

				<h2>4. What Filosign provides</h2>
				<p>
					Filosign provides software for sending, viewing, signing, storing,
					and exporting proof records for encrypted document workflows. Optional
					features may let approved workspaces attach optional payout rules
					that execute through public smart contracts on supported networks.
				</p>
				<p>
					Filosign does not provide legal, tax, accounting, payroll,
					identity-verification, fund-holding, custodial wallet, money transmission,
					or regulated financial services.
				</p>

				<h2>5. Electronic records and signatures</h2>
				<p>
					By using Filosign to send, acknowledge, or sign a document, you
					consent to using electronic records and electronic signatures for that
					workflow. You agree that clicking signing controls, authorizing wallet
					signatures, or otherwise completing a signing step may be used as
					evidence of your intent to sign.
				</p>
				<p>
					Filosign records off-chain acknowledgement, document-view, and signing
					timestamps for participant workflows to support audit trails.
				</p>
				<p>
					Filosign is designed to support evidence of intent, attribution,
					integrity, timestamps, and record retention. You are responsible for
					deciding whether a Filosign workflow is valid and appropriate for your
					document, counterparty, jurisdiction, and required legal standard. See our
					<a href="/legal/e-signature-validity" class="underline"
						>E-signature Validity</a
					> page for more context (not legal advice).
				</p>

				<h2>6. Excluded and high-risk documents</h2>
				<p>
					{EXCLUDED_DOCUMENTS_INTRO_TERMS}
				</p>
				<ExcludedDocumentsList />

				<h2>7. Document and data responsibility</h2>
				<p>
					You are responsible for the legality, accuracy, confidentiality, and
					suitability of documents you upload, send, view, sign, store, or
					export through Filosign. Filosign does not review document contents for
					legal sufficiency.
				</p>
				<p>
					Documents are designed to be encrypted before upload. Filosign still
					processes metadata, participant data, wallet addresses, transaction
					hashes, and operational records needed to run the service.
				</p>

				<h2>8. Subscriptions, billing, and refunds</h2>
				<p>
					Paid plans may be billed monthly or annually. <strong
						>{DODO_PAYMENTS.name}</strong
					> acts as the <strong>Merchant of Record</strong> for subscription checkout:
					it is the legal seller on the charge, handles applicable tax calculation
					and remittance, and processes payment operations. Filosign provisions your
					plan using identifiers and status we receive from Dodo (such as customer
					id, plan, and subscription state). Payment card and checkout data are processed
					by Dodo under <a
						href={DODO_PAYMENTS.privacyPolicyUrl}
						class="underline"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">Dodo's privacy policy</a
					> as an independent controller.
				</p>
				<p>
					Fees are non-refundable except where required by law, required by Dodo as
					Merchant of Record, or approved by Filosign support. If you bought the wrong
					plan, forgot to cancel, or believe a charge was made in error, contact
					<a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_OPERATOR.supportEmail}`} class="underline"
						>{LEGAL_OPERATOR.supportEmail}</a
					> within 7 days. We may grant goodwill refunds for legitimate mistakes at our
					discretion.
				</p>
				<p>
					Cancelling a subscription prevents future renewals but does not
					automatically refund the current billing period.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Payment Disputes and Chargebacks:</strong> Contact
					{LEGAL_OPERATOR.supportEmail} to resolve product or access issues before
					disputing a charge with your bank when possible. Filing a dispute or chargeback
					without contacting us first could result in suspension of your account, paid
					features, and payout attachment access while the dispute is reviewed. Repeated or
					fraudulent disputes may lead to permanent termination. We will preserve reasonable
					access to export your existing signed documents and proofs where operationally
					and legally permitted.
				</p>

				<h2>9. Optional payout attachment</h2>
				<p>
					Filosign may provide software and optional transaction relay so a sender can
					attach <strong>optional USDC payout instructions</strong> to a document.
					The feature is optional. It requires a paid plan, manual workspace approval,
					and acceptance of the
					<a href="/legal/settlement-feature-addendum" class="underline"
						>Payout attachment addendum</a
					>. Production use is USDC on Base. See
					<a href="/legal/non-custodial-settlement" class="underline"
						>Payout attachment</a
					> for a plain-language overview.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Not a payment service.</strong> Filosign is not a bank, money
					transmitter, escrow agent, or payment guarantor. Transfers, when they occur,
					move between user wallets. Filosign is not a party to those transfers and does
					not resolve payment disputes between senders and recipients.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Software access is not custody.</strong> We do not hold, pool, custody,
					transmit, or control your funds. Your assets stay in your self-custodied wallet.
					We cannot access, freeze, block, or reverse them. You can use the blockchain
					without our app. We may still suspend or limit access to Filosign software
					(UI, API, relay) for security, compliance, abuse, or operations.
				</p>
				<p>
					Payout attachment uses a pull-payment model: you register rules on-chain and
					approve the on-chain payout contract from your wallet:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>You control token approvals and wallet transactions.</li>
					<li>Filosign does not approve, custody, or reverse funds for you.</li>
					<li>Filosign does not charge payout-volume fees.</li>
					<li>
						You may revoke funding by setting token approval to zero before a leg
						executes.
					</li>
					<li>
						You may cancel remaining unpaid legs before a rule is fully executed; amounts
						already transferred on-chain cannot be reversed by Filosign.
					</li>
					<li>
						Legs may execute independently. Signing a document does not ensure any
						attached payout will complete.
					</li>
					<li>
						After the first required signer signs on-chain, payers generally cannot
						change payout terms through the validator.
					</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					You are responsible for wallet security, recipients, approvals, taxes,
					invoices, accounting, legality, and funds you send or receive. Blockchain
					transactions may be public and irreversible. Recipients have no payment
					guarantee from Filosign.
				</p>

				<h2>10. Supported path vs. direct contract use</h2>
				<p>
					The supported path is payout-attached workflows through the Filosign app or
					API. On that path, we may enforce product rules, index status, and include
					records in proof exports. Direct contract use on-chain is still possible, but
					Filosign does not guarantee policy enforcement, indexing, or automation for
					those transactions.
				</p>

				<h2>11. Prohibited use</h2>
				<p>
					You must comply with the <a href="/acceptable-use" class="underline"
						>Acceptable Use Policy</a
					>. Prohibited conduct includes fraud, sanctions evasion, illegal payments,
					unauthorized document sharing, malware, harassment, and any activity that
					violates applicable law or the Acceptable Use Policy.
				</p>

				<h2>12. Automation and availability</h2>
				<p>
					Filosign may relay supported payout transactions when conditions are met, but
					does not guarantee execution. Transfers may fail due to insufficient balance,
					revoked approval, network issues, unmet conditions, or smart contract or network
					risk.
				</p>
				<p>
					The service is provided as available. Filosign does not currently
					offer uptime, support, recovery-time, or service-level commitments.
				</p>

				<h2>13. Suspension and termination</h2>
				<p>
					We may suspend, limit, or terminate access if we believe your use
					creates legal, security, payment, sanctions, fraud, abuse, or
					operational risk. We may restrict payout attachment separately from document
					features.
				</p>

				<h2>14. Intellectual property</h2>
				<p>
					Filosign and its licensors own the Service, software, branding, and
					documentation. We grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable
					license to use the Service during an active account or permitted trial,
					subject to these Terms.
				</p>
				<p>
					You retain ownership of documents and content you upload. You grant
					Filosign a license to host, encrypt, transmit, display, and process your
					content only as needed to operate the Service, provide support, enforce
					these Terms, and comply with law.
				</p>
				<p>
					If you provide feedback or suggestions, you grant us a perpetual,
					royalty-free license to use them without restriction or compensation.
				</p>

				<h2>15. Indemnification</h2>
				<p>
					To the maximum extent permitted by law, you will defend, indemnify, and
					hold harmless {LEGAL_OPERATOR.tradingName}, and its affiliates and personnel, from claims,
					damages, losses, and expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising
					from your content, your use of the Service, your violation of these Terms
					or the Acceptable Use Policy, or your violation of applicable law or
					third-party rights.
				</p>

				<h2>16. Export controls and sanctions</h2>
				<p>
					You may not use the Service in violation of applicable export control,
					sanctions, or trade laws. You represent that you are not located in, organized
					under, or ordinarily resident in a comprehensively sanctioned jurisdiction,
					and are not a prohibited or restricted party under applicable sanctions lists,
					unless authorized by law.
				</p>

				<h2>17. Third-party services</h2>
				<p>
					The Service integrates with third parties such as wallet providers,
					blockchain networks, email providers, analytics tools, hosting providers,
					and {DODO_PAYMENTS.name}. Your use of those services may be subject to
					separate terms. See our <a href="/subprocessors" class="underline"
						>Subprocessors</a
					> page for providers that process personal data on our behalf.
				</p>

				<h2>18. Changes to these Terms</h2>
				<p>
					We may update these Terms from time to time. We will post the updated
					Terms on this page and update the "Last updated" date. Material changes
					may also be notified through the Service or by email where appropriate.
					Continued use after the effective date constitutes acceptance of the
					updated Terms, except where prohibited by law.
				</p>

				<h2>19. Disclaimers and limitation of liability</h2>
				<p>
					To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Service is provided "as is"
					and "as available" without warranties of any kind, whether express,
					implied, or statutory, including merchantability, fitness for a
					particular purpose, and non-infringement.
				</p>
				<p>
					To the maximum extent permitted by law, {LEGAL_OPERATOR.tradingName} will not be liable for indirect, incidental,
					special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive damages; lost profits; lost
					data; failed transactions; wallet compromise; or third-party service failures.
				</p>
				<p>
					To the maximum extent permitted by law, our total aggregate liability for
					claims arising out of or relating to the Service or these Terms is limited
					to the greater of (a) amounts you paid to Filosign for the Service in the
					twelve (12) months before the event giving rise to liability, or (b) one
					hundred U.S. dollars (USD $100). Some jurisdictions do not allow certain
					limitations; in those cases, the limit applies to the fullest extent permitted.
				</p>

				<h2>20. Governing Law and Dispute Resolution</h2>
				<p>
					These Terms and any dispute, claim, or controversy arising out of or in
					connection with them or your use of the Service shall be governed by, and
					construed in accordance with, the laws of the Republic of India, with jurisdiction
					and venue in the courts of {LEGAL_OPERATOR.location}.
				</p>
				<p>
					Any dispute arising out of or in connection with these Terms, including any
					question regarding their existence, validity, or termination, shall be referred
					to and finally resolved by arbitration in {LEGAL_OPERATOR.location}, in accordance with the
					Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996. The arbitral tribunal shall consist of a sole arbitrator
					appointed by mutual agreement, or failing agreement, in accordance with the Act.
					The language of the arbitration shall be English.
				</p>

				<h2>21. General</h2>
				<p>
					If any provision is held invalid, the remaining provisions remain in effect.
					Our failure to enforce a provision is not a waiver. You may not assign these
					Terms without our consent; we may assign them in connection with a merger,
					acquisition, or sale of assets. These Terms, together with the Privacy Policy,
					Acceptable Use Policy, and documents incorporated by reference, are the entire
					agreement regarding the Service.
				</p>

				<h2>22. Contact</h2>
				<p>
					Contact us at
					<a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_OPERATOR.supportEmail}`} class="underline"
						>{LEGAL_OPERATOR.supportEmail}</a
					>. See also our <a href="/privacy" class="underline">Privacy Policy</a>,
					<a href="/acceptable-use" class="underline">Acceptable Use Policy</a>,
					<a href="/subprocessors" class="underline">Subprocessors</a>, and
					<a href="/legal/non-custodial-settlement" class="underline"
						>Payout attachment</a
					>, and
					<a href="/legal/settlement-feature-addendum" class="underline"
						>Payout attachment addendum</a
					>.
				</p>
			</LegalDocument>
	</MarketingPageShell>
</BaseLayout>
